{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe 12 `infra/scripts` files below contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale prose identified by the comment audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. Shortening it must not obscure operational, security, or recovery contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve executable text and behavior-bearing directives byte-for-byte. Replace narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer.\n\n## Scope\n- `autodeploy.sh` — Preserve independent component markers/backoffs, no advancement on incomplete deployment, bounded ports/memory/drain, secrets-before-start, candidate validation, exact nginx rollback, observability/certbot deployment, and distinct deploy-versus-detect trigger sets.\n- `bootstrap-gerrit-admin.sh` — Preserve fresh pre-OAuth bootstrap, orphan NoteDb branch creation, idempotent public-key installation, account checks, restart requirement, and public `ADMIN_PUBKEY`.\n- `compose-up.sh` — Preserve four-service startup; side-effect-free volume enumeration; Docker, journald, `/var/tmp`, and writable-container cap installers before first Docker start; and their nonfatal failure posture. Preserve that the reaper removes only exited/unowned debris, running layers remain uncapped, and hard overlay2 quotas require XFS `pquota` plus reboot. Preserve parent-only gate-scratch setup and warning—downstream gate admission, not compose-up, refuses a missing marker—plus plugin/hook seeding, OAuth, and materializer-specific failure postures.\n- `config-check.sh` — Preserve daemon-independent YAML validation, side-effect-free external-volume comparison, loud empty-enumeration failure, and embedded negative tests.\n- `fetch-secrets.sh` — Preserve PAT fallback asymmetry, blank-key semantics, static-token fail-closed behavior, Jira soft degradation, atomic permissioned writes, nonlogging, and both gitleaks directives. Do not call `MCP_HMAC_SIGNING_KEY` a current verdict signer.\n- `install-autodeploy.sh` and `install-certbot-timer.sh` — Preserve idempotent installation, mirror/bootstrap and disabled-timer posture, host-nginx/dnf/venv fallback, HTTP-01 webroot, renewal/reload cadence, and arguments.\n- `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` — Preserve seed-only-if-absent behavior, at-least-one-server validation, optional reload, and intentional 502 posture; do not claim target-format validation or atomic generation.\n- `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` — Preserve raw guard handling, `umask 077`, unrelated env entries, atomic env replacement, direct nginx-map write, deny-all fallback, brief rotation 403, and the application's second header check.\n- `mcp-entrypoint.sh` — Preserve asynchronous provisioning, uninitialized-until-converged reads, safe clearing, directory-inode locking, resolvable-HEAD double-check, blobless anonymous clone, URL-scoped credential helper, PID-1 `exec`, and its exact shellcheck directive.\n- `observability.sh` — Preserve bounded network/Docker/du/journal reads; per-metric failure semantics; MCP 401 health; whole-Docker-root accounting against the four known ledger rows; and one `docker system df` census shared by storage and writable-layer metrics. Preserve independent writable total, exited/reclaimable bytes, shared-budget percent, reaper heartbeat, and non-alarmed quota-enforceability publication; the reaper does not bound running layers. Preserve source single-sourcing, dimension/alarm parity, cursor safety, publish-before-cursor advancement, mirror failure=`1`, and final exit `0`. Retain intentional fail-safe zero/100 values and state heartbeats rather than claiming “no fabricated zeroes.”\n- `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` — Preserve durable clone setup, global identity, same-epoch merge-as-union, narrowly guarded epoch adoption, and ensure-registry invocation; never reset to a moving ref or discard local work.\n\nConsumers include systemd, deployment/config gates, nginx, containers, CloudWatch alarms, security checks, and operators. `compose-up.sh` is also an autodeploy detect-only materializer path; `observability.sh` is reinstalled through `OBS_PATHS` and feeds the container alarms. Preserve every shebang and exact shellcheck, gitleaks, tickets-boundary, raw-git, and related policy directive.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only the permitted comments/docstrings or blank lines in the declared files; executable/configuration data and exact behavior-bearing directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked TSV semantic matrix authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, stale, or historical prose was removed while current rationale remained.\n- [ ] Recorded focused checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] Missing or FAIL semantic rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded content-only guards, focused checks, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint. The independent matrix, not exact prose matching, judges semantic preservation."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788609398016787001,"uuid":"eb88b3e3-018c-48bc-a2bb-756b8ac41bd6"}